    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a structured address form to the create/update owner flow, keeping the flat `address` field fully backward-compatible.\n\n**Contract (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)**\n- Added optional `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` properties to the `OwnerFields` schema (which the `Owner` response schema inherits), and documented `address` as the composed/normalized output.\n- Removed `address` from the required list, since an owner may now supply its address via either form. `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone` remain required \u2014 so earlier minimal owners are still accepted.\n\n**Persistence**\n- `Owner` entity: new `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` fields with `address_line1` / `address_line2` columns and accessors.\n- Added the two nullable columns to all four DB schemas (h2 \u2014 the active profile \u2014 plus hsqldb, mysql, postgres).\n\n**Logic**\n- `OwnerAddress.compose(addressLine1, addressLine2, address)`: prefers the structured form when `addressLine1` is non-blank, returning the normalized `addressLine1` with a single space + normalized `addressLine2` appended when present; otherwise falls back to the normalized flat `address`; returns `null` when neither form supplies an address.\n- `ValidateOwnerFields` (POST): normalizes each supplied part, composes the effective `address`, rejects with the `address` field error only when neither form yields a value, and stores the normalized lines + composed address back on the body.\n- `ApplyOwner` (PUT): same structured-preferred composition for consistency.\n\nEverything downstream that reads the address reads the composed `address` (structured-when-present, flat-fallback), while `city` and `postcode` \u2014 the structured components used by the household hash, postcode validation and locality \u2014 flow through as before.\n\nThe MapStruct mapper auto-maps the new fields in both directions, and the generated DTO/mapper were verified to carry `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` end to end.",
